When running in Codex, use Codex for every delegated task, including screeners,
advisors, and reviewers. This provider policy overrides conflicting provider and
model requirements in shared skills and agent definitions, including Opus pins.
Use the parent's Codex model or a smaller available Codex model suited to the task.
Use Claude or another provider only when explicitly requested in the conversation.
If Codex delegation is unavailable, keep the work in the parent instead of switching
providers. Include this provider policy in every child agent's brief so it applies
to any further delegation.

